[size=5][b]Unique Mechanics[/b][/size]

[b]Two layers, not one.[/b] The ancestor bond and your Reclamation focus are separate and both matter. The ancestors are your constant floor; the Reclamation you favor is your ceiling. You feed them with different deeds, and they answer in different ways - the ancestors with a steadying ward against magic, your Reclamation with its own gifts of mind, blade, or shadow.

[b]The urn goes where you go.[/b] The whole ancestor practice fits in your pocket. There is no shrine to walk to and no tomb to find: the rite is an item in your inventory, and it works in a bandit camp or on a mountainside as well as it works at home. What home adds is depth, and the watch the dead keep over you until dawn.

[b]The ancestors never erode.[/b] Alone among devotion layers, the ancestor bond has no passive decay. A Dunmer far from home, with no tomb to tend, is not punished for the distance. Keep the rites and the bond deepens; let them slide and it simply grows quiet, waiting for you to return.

[b]The three pull against each other.[/b] Azura, Boethiah, and Mephala do not want the same Dunmer. Broad worship is comfortable and it stops at Devoted. Committing to one means accepting that the other two will find your new habits distasteful - and that is precisely why a focused Reclamation feels like a decision rather than a grind.

[size=5][b]If You Are Cursed (Vampire or Werewolf)[/b][/size]

[b]Vampire - the ancestors fall silent.[/b] This is one of the most striking moments in the mod. To the honored dead, undeath is a wound in the cycle, and they will not speak to what you have become. Your ancestor bond goes silent: the urn stops answering, the rites score nothing, and the dead withdraw their strength - your Maximum Magicka is reduced by 10 for as long as the silence holds. Curing the vampirism restores the connection and lifts the penalty, but the ancestors remember the silence, and a permanent scar remains. With the ancestors muted, Boethiah and Mephala draw closer, and the road to Molag Bal opens, but none of that fills the hollow where your dead used to be.

[b]Werewolf - ritually unclean.[/b] The beast-blood does not silence the ancestors, but it makes you unclean in their sight. The rites still answer, at half their worth, and your Reclamation is lightly strained as well. No new Daedric road opens to comfort you - Hircine has no place in Dunmer faith. It is a strain to be endured and, in time, cured, not a path to walk.

[size=5][b]Quick Reference[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Gods:[/b] the Ancestors (always), plus the three Reclamations - Azura, Boethiah, Mephala. Other Princes are deviation, not worship.
[*][b]Starting choice:[/b] none - both layers run from the start. You later focus one Reclamation (via that god's offer) to reach Champion.
[*][b]Top 3 ways to gain:[/b] pray over the ancestral urn in your Miscellaneous tab, once a day, and at dawn or dusk when you can; do the deeds your chosen Reclamation actually cares about; read her sacred books and finish her artifact quest.
[*][b]Main ways to lose:[/b] living against the creed of the god you chose; defying Azura over the Black Star; the Devoted cap on broad worship. Ancestor distance costs you nothing.
[*][b]Rough days to Champion:[/b] about 30 to 45 days of normal play, roughly 20 if you commit hard to one Reclamation; the ancestor bond reaches full strength in about three in-game weeks of daily rites.
[/list]
